  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"law\": in some languages one word means both *law* (the system) and *a right* (something you are allowed to have or do); English keeps **law** and **right** apart.",
    "grammar": "\"law\" as the whole system takes **the** (*obey the law*); as a subject it takes no article (*study law*); as one rule it is countable (*a new law*).",
